==Battleground==
*2 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 12~14 seconds<sup>360f~420f</sup>.
**5 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is a relatively normal stage, as it is a simple army of strong enemies without the help of [[Long Distance]], [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] trait, [[Burrow|burrowing]]/[[Revive|reviving]], [[:Category:Omni Strike Enemies|Omni Strike]], etc.

Even then, this stage should not be underestimated. Constantly buffed Scissoroos and Ursamajors can push very hard, especially if the Ursamajors are strengthened. Hypermaxing [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] will prove to be incredibly useful since it allows him to tank 1 hit from Scissoroo, making the startoff much easier.

For this reason, all you need to have from the previous stage is a bunch of strong units with good enough range for Ursamajor (or, better, [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]) and some meatshields. Due to the strength of the enemies, however, you shouldn't take this level lightly, especially if you don't bring [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien units]] like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]].

